Explanation

This text is provided as explanation only. The licence itself begins at the line starting with 'MAGICC8+ Licence'.

The licence is a 3-Clause BSD licence with a single additional clause, the MAGICC clause. The point of this clause is to make sure that use of modified versions of MAGICC is clearly linked to the modified version. This clarity will help reduce confusion about which version of MAGICC was used in different pieces of analysis (e.g. papers), ensure that MAGICC developers are aware of work being done within the wider MAGICC ecosystem and ensure that results are reproducible (thanks to the specification of parameter values on top of core code).

The clause does not introduce any requirements for users of unmodified versions of MAGICC beyond those specified by the 3-Clause BSD licence. Put another way: if you want to use MAGICC without modification, then the same rules apply as under the 3-Clause BSD licence.


